  "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=4{x}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (20{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =20{x}^{4}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =20{x}^{4}{e}^{4{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
